// Title: Potential Mftrace.EXE Abuse
// Sigma ID: 3d48c9d3-1aa6-418d-98d3-8fd3c01a564e
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-06-09 | Modified: 2023-08-03
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127
// Description: Detects child processes of the "Trace log generation tool for Media Foundation Tools"
//   (Mftrace.exe) which can abused to execute arbitrary binaries.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use for tracing purposes
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Mftrace/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_mftrace_child_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\mftrace.exe"
